       <item>
        <widget class="QLabel" name="label_72">
         <property name="text">
          <string>Defining Surfaces</string>
         </property>
         <property name="alignment">
          <set>Qt::AlignmentFlag::AlignCenter</set>
         </property>
        </widget>
       </item>
       <item>
        <widget class="QPlainTextEdit" name="kcfg_srfDefineCfg">
         <property name="sizePolicy">
          <sizepolicy hsizetype="Expanding" vsizetype="Fixed">
           <horstretch>0</horstretch>
           <verstretch>0</verstretch>
          </sizepolicy>
         </property>
         <property name="minimumSize">
          <size>
           <width>0</width>
           <height>300</height>
          </size>
         </property>
         <property name="toolTip">
          <string>&lt;html&gt;&lt;head/&gt;&lt;body&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-size:12pt;&quot;&gt;Surface is combination of three parameters: Screen(Output) name and optional VirtualDesktops and ActivityId. For example:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-size:12pt; font-weight:700;&quot;&gt;HDMI-A-1:Desktop 1:99e10d31-e8f3-44aa-bbed-2a543f13fa54- &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-size:12pt;&quot;&gt;this uniquely defines one surface, another example defines group of surfaces: &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-size:12pt; font-weight:700;&quot;&gt;DP-2 &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-size:12pt;&quot;&gt;- this include all surfaces with any activities and virtual desktops on monitor DP-2. To define a surface for further use in program configuration use the next format: &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-size:12pt; font-weight:700;&quot;&gt;label=&amp;lt;outputName&amp;gt;,&amp;lt;outputName&amp;gt;...[:&amp;lt;virtualDesktop&amp;gt;,&amp;lt;virtualDesktop&amp;gt;...[:&amp;lt;activityId&amp;gt;]] &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-size:12pt;&quot;&gt;For example:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-size:12pt; font-weight:700;&quot;&gt; allMonitors=: &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-size:12pt;&quot;&gt;to make label for all monitors or&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-size:12pt; font-weight:700;&quot;&gt; mainScreen=HDMI-A-1,DP-2:Desktop 1 &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-size:12pt;&quot;&gt;in another parts of Krohnkite config you can use &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-size:12pt; font-weight:700;&quot;&gt;mainMonitor&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-size:12pt;&quot;&gt; as surface name(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-size:12pt; font-weight:700;&quot;&gt;All Case Sensitive)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-size:12pt;&quot;&gt;.Please note that there may be multiple monitor names, separated by commas as in the example, or there may be none. The first one has higher priority and if this monitor works in this moment the surface in example will belong ONLY him NOT BOTH.This can be useful if you apply monitor to your notebook for example and you want the monitor to have this config. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;</string>
         </property>
         <property name="inputMethodHints">
          <set>Qt::InputMethodHint::ImhMultiLine</set>
         </property>
        </widget>
       </item>
       <item>
        <widget class="QLabel" name="label_73">
         <property name="text">
          <string>Surfaces Configuration</string>
         </property>
         <property name="alignment">
          <set>Qt::AlignmentFlag::AlignCenter</set>
         </property>
        </widget>
       </item>
       <item>
        <widget class="QPlainTextEdit" name="kcfg_srfDefaultConfig">
         <property name="sizePolicy">
          <sizepolicy hsizetype="Expanding" vsizetype="Fixed">
           <horstretch>0</horstretch>
           <verstretch>0</verstretch>
          </sizepolicy>
         </property>
         <property name="minimumSize">
          <size>
           <width>0</width>
           <height>300</height>
          </size>
         </property>
         <property name="toolTip">
          <string>&lt;html&gt;&lt;head/&gt;&lt;body&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-size:12pt;&quot;&gt;Overriding default parameters for every surface. Format: &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-size:12pt; font-weight:700;&quot;&gt;SrfLabel:param=value,param=value... &amp;lt;Enter&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-size:12pt;&quot;&gt;Possible parameters(case insensetive): &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-size:12pt; font-weight:700;&quot;&gt;capacity&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-size:12pt;&quot;&gt; or &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-size:12pt; font-weight:700;&quot;&gt;cp; overcapacity &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-size:12pt;&quot;&gt;or&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-size:12pt; font-weight:700;&quot;&gt; oc &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;For example: &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-size:12pt; font-weight:700;&quot;&gt;primaryScreen:cp=6,oc=false&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-size:12pt;&quot;&gt;Next example set capacity on surface(s)  with Label = primaryScreen  and disable overcapacity windows movement on them.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;</string>
         </property>
        </widget>
       </item>
       <item>
        <spacer name="verticalSpacer_2">
         <property name="orientation">
          <enum>Qt::Orientation::Vertical</enum>
         </property>
         <property name="sizeHint" stdset="0">
          <size>
           <width>20</width>
           <height>40</height>
          </size>
         </property>
        </spacer>
       </item>
      </layout>
     </widget>
