          <item>
           <widget class="QLineEdit" name="kcfg_soleWindowOutputOverride">
            <property name="toolTip">
             <string>&lt;html&gt;&lt;head/&gt;&lt;body&gt;&lt;p&gt;Comma-separated list to override the default Sole Window properties parameters: OutputName:Width:Height:NoBorders:NoGaps. Width and Height in % and can be from 1 to 100, NoBorders and NoGaps can be 0 or 1. You can omit parameters for example &lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:700;&quot;&gt;DP-1:50&lt;/span&gt; means you override only width to 50% on &lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:700;&quot;&gt;DP-1&lt;/span&gt; monitor. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Note. If you enable the No Gap option, this means that width and height no longer matter.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Two monitors example:&lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:700;&quot;&gt; DP-1:::1:1,DP-2:80:70&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;on&lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:700;&quot;&gt; DP-1 &lt;/span&gt;no Borders nor Gaps, on DP-2: 80% Width and 70% Height&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;</string>
            </property>
            <property name="placeholderText">
             <string>OutputName:Width:Height,NoBorders,NoGaps,...</string>
            </property>
           </widget>
          </item>
         </layout>
        </widget>
